    "result_text": "All 262 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. (The stack traces in the log are from tests that assert on expected error responses; their reported results are 0 failures/0 errors.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts **1 July**), driven off the already-business-day-adjusted `registrationDate` stored on the owner.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec):\n- Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` field (`FY<YY>`).\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` description to say its year segment is the fiscal year.\n- Updated the `membershipPoints` description: the tenure bonus now depends on elapsed fiscal years, not a 365-day window.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**:\n- Added a `fiscalYear` mapping plus `formatFiscalYear(owner)` \u2192 `\"FY%02d\"` of the fiscal-year start year.\n- Added a private `fiscalYearStart(date)` helper: returns the date's year when the month is \u2265 July, otherwise the previous year.\n- `formatMembershipNumber` now uses `fiscalYearStart(registrationDate) % 100` for the `M<YY>` segment instead of the calendar year.\n- `formatMembershipPoints` tenure bonus (+3) now triggers when `fiscalYearStart(now) - fiscalYearStart(registrationDate) >= 1` \u2014 i.e. the registration and current dates fall in different fiscal years \u2014 replacing the old `plusDays(365)` check.\n\n**Semantic choices** (nothing in the tests pinned exact values beyond the `FY\\d{2}` regex, so I picked the standard, internally consistent reading and documented it in both the spec and the Javadoc):\n- A fiscal year is labelled by its **starting** calendar year, so e.g. 5 Aug 2026 \u2192 `FY26`, 3 Mar 2026 \u2192 `FY25`.\n- \"Tenure in elapsed fiscal years\" = number of 1-July boundaries crossed between registration and now; the bonus applies at \u2265 1.\n\nThe `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, and the tenure component of `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel` all now derive from the same fiscal-year helper, keeping them consistent.",
